      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, that makes sense. so by tapering the edges, you're basically smoothing out those discontinuities that cause the leakage.\n\nbut i'm still a bit confused about the trade-offs. if windowing helps with leakage, why don't we just use a super aggressive window that goes to zero really fast to completely eliminate the edges? what's the catch? like, does it mess with the frequency resolution or something?",
